    {
      "kind": "topic",
      "text": "### 5.1 Start with a uniform interface",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000225"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [],
      "fills": [],
      "need": "",
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source",
      "chunkId": "c0003-flat-05",
      "annotations": [
        "repair_source_fallback"
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "source",
      "text": "Every fragment has an interface: one incoming wire at the top and zero or more outgoing wires at the bottom. The outermost fragment hangs from a single root. Free variables—names no surrounding λ owns—become named interface nodes. That stable shape lets you plug a fragment into its parent the way a function plugs into a call.",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000226"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [],
      "fills": [],
      "need": "",
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source",
      "chunkId": "c0003-flat-05",
      "annotations": [
        "repair_source_fallback"
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "source",
      "text": "abstraction fragment [λx.M]ℓ",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
        "u000227"
      ],
      "defines": [],
      "requires": [],
      "mentions": [],
      "fills": [],
      "need": "",
      "gapType": null,
      "origin": "source",
      "chunkId": "c0003-flat-05",
      "annotations": [
        "repair_source_fallback"
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "source",
      "text": "flowchart TB\nrootA((root))\nlam@{ shape: triangle, label: \"λ\" }\nRx@{ shape: trapezoid, label: \"Rₓ\" }\nM@{ shape: rect, label: \"[M]ℓ body\" }\nuses@{ shape: rect, label: \"bound uses\" }\nrootA -->|principal · parent| lam\nlam ---|2nd aux · variable → principal| Rx\nlam ---|1st aux · body| M\nRx ---|auxiliary ports| uses\nM ~~~ Rx",
      "sourceUnitIds": [
